  "experiments": [
    "First geometry candidate passed 237/348; linear routes and controls raised this to 308/350.",
    "A rigid-hop port passed 329/350. Direct per-hop captures isolated the remaining FK4 and HADEC signs. A casacore 3.7.1 C++ probe reproduced CASA and traced the direct APP FK4 mismatch to MeasMath::applyETerms default epoch argument 2000.0.",
    "The 0.142 nT IGRF residual came from decimal-year interpolation instead of MeasTable::IGRF fractional MJD. The 0.203 mm Earth-radius position residual traced to the moment LAST is rounded by MCFrame::getLASTr. Both corrected before recapture.",
    "Running the old CASA capture on the bundled snapshot showed three failures (up to 0.0186 m). CASA with the same bundled snapshot removes those test-input mismatches at the original tolerances.",
    "Initial 362-case candidate passed and was faster for all 20 measured calls. Its absolute tolerance masked unrotated tiny magnetic vectors, and review found five issues.",
    "Physical-strength and missing-frame captures plus the sentinel-radius regression failed 21 of 380 cases with the reviewed code. The first repair passed 378, with both APP-to-B1950 direction controls failing.",
    "A casacore 3.7.1 stage probe measured a first inverse E-term residual of 1.68694e-5, above the 1e-5 threshold, and a second of 3.35921e-10. Normalizing the second iterate reproduces the CASA direction control."
  ],
  "review": {
    "state": "resolved",
    "scope": "One fresh-context Astra xhigh shared-code review of 6946e1c3e6. Verified the five repairs with independent cases.",
    "findings": [
      "Convert explicit magnetic fields to ITRF coordinates for an IGRF output.",
      "Serialize and display baseline, UVW and magnetic magnitudes without the position height sentinel.",
      "Match both magnetic reference-code mappings to casacore's independent enum constants.",
      "Obtain the apparent phase centre for terrestrial UVW hops, requiring the frame elements CASA uses.",
      "Use the direct FK4 apparent route and preserve field norm through direction corrections."
    ]
  },
